`coco_pipe.utils.NoDataError` (a `RuntimeError`, also in `coco_pipe.io`) means an empty selection: the BIDS loader raises it when no recording has the requested events and none failed to load, and `load_descriptor_table` when no row is left, so callers can tell it from a failure without reading the message. `coco_pipe.utils.resolve_device` is the one device rule of the foundation models and the topological reducer, and refuses a CUDA device when CUDA is not available; an extractor on such a device refuses to be built, instead of failing at the first recording.
